IMPORT_FROM_FILE: L3_element_design_concept.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
**Level 3 of 4 - Element Design Concept.**

The non-technical design of **one element**, described in enough detail to
implement it. An element can be a smartphone app, a web app, a server element,
or a whole complicated system. This document covers `TBD`, declared at L2.

One L3 document per element. Record the L2 element ID in `METADATA`.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
UID: L3-APPLICABILITY
TITLE: Which sections apply to this element

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Not all sections apply to every element type. Set `ELEMENT_PROFILE` in the
document metadata, then state below which sections apply here and why - so a
reader can tell an omission was a decision.

**User-facing frontend** (web app, mobile app, kiosk)
All sections apply. User interfaces and use cases are the core. Technical
interfaces describe inbound calls from users and outbound calls to backend
services. Technical functions cover rendering logic, validation and local state
management.

**Backend service / API** (application server, microservice)
Goals, use cases, both technical interface sections, technical functions and
entities are the core. User interfaces typically do not apply. Quality
requirements and constraints are particularly important.

**Integration / middleware** (adapter, message broker, API gateway)
Technical interfaces inbound and outbound are the core. Use cases may be limited
or absent. Focus on data transformation, routing logic in technical functions,
and error handling. Entities describe the structures being passed through.

**Hardware-bound element** (embedded device, display terminal, sensor gateway)
Goals and constraints are central. Technical interfaces describe physical
protocols and data formats. Use cases cover operational modes and interactions.
User interfaces apply only if the device has a local UI. Technical functions
cover device-specific logic - firmware triggers, signal processing.

**When in doubt**, start with goals and use cases to establish what the element
must achieve, then add only the sections where there is meaningful content. An
empty section is less useful than a focused, well-populated set.

| Section | Applies | Note |
|---|---|---|
| Goals (`G-`) | TBD | |
| Use cases (`UC-`) | TBD | |
| User interfaces (`UI-`) | TBD | |
| Technical functions (`TF-`) | TBD | |
| Technical interfaces inbound (`TI-`) | TBD | |
| Technical interfaces outbound (`TO-`) | TBD | |
| Entities (`E-`) | TBD | |
| Quality requirements (`QR-`) | TBD | |
| Constraints (`C-`) | TBD | |
<<<

