[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: L3-UI
TITLE: User interfaces

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
A user interface gives a user access to the element's functionality. The focus
is on what is **visible**, what data is displayed, and what actions are
available - not on the implementation of those actions.

**Detailed behaviour belongs elsewhere.** Which functions are called, how data
is processed, how errors are handled, what happens next - all of that is in the
referenced use cases and technical functions, not here.

**Reference a use case** for user-facing multi-step actions with feedback.
**Reference a technical function** for instant data operations.
<<<

[USER_INTERFACE]
UID: UI-01
STATUS: Draft
USER_TYPE: TBD - name the L2 user type that may use this
TITLE: TBD
STATEMENT: >>>
TBD - What this interface is for.
<<<
VISIBLE_DATA: >>>
TBD - For each piece of data shown:

- **attributeName** (dataType): what is displayed
  Source: [LINK: E-01] attribute `E-01.1`, or [LINK: TF-01]
  Conditions: when it is visible, or how it changes with state
<<<
ACTIONS: >>>
TBD - For each available action:

- **Action name**: what it represents - button press, link, selection
  Related use case: [LINK: UC-01]
  Or, for a simple instant operation, related function: [LINK: TF-01]
  Conditions: when it is available, e.g. "enabled only when fields are filled"
<<<
INPUT_FIELDS: >>>
TBD - *If applicable.* For each field where the user enters data:

- **fieldName** (dataType): what the user enters
  Validation: UI-level only - required, format, length
  Related use case: [LINK: UC-01]
<<<
NAVIGATION: >>>
TBD - *If applicable.* For each navigation target:

- Target: [LINK: UI-01] - when navigation occurs
  Related use case describing the flow: [LINK: UC-01]
<<<
