[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: L3-TI
TITLE: Technical interfaces (inbound)

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Interfaces this element **provides** so other elements can access its data or
functionality.
<<<

[TECHNICAL_INTERFACE_IN]
UID: TI-01
CALL_TYPE: Synchronous
STATUS: Draft
PROTOCOL: TBD
TITLE: TBD
STATEMENT: >>>
TBD - What this interface is for.
<<<
CALLING_ELEMENTS: >>>
TBD - Elements that may call this, with their outbound interface where
documented: "[Element name] ([LINK: SE-01], TO-nn)"
<<<
INPUT: >>>
TBD - For each parameter:
- **parameterName** (dataType, required/optional): description
<<<
OUTPUT: >>>
TBD - For each output value:
- **outputName** (dataType): description, and the conditions under which it is
  returned
<<<
ACTION: >>>
TBD - What the interface does, at a high level.

*Simple interface:* reference the function implementing it - "Calls
[LINK: TF-01] with the provided input and returns the result."

*Complex interface, or no single function:* which entities are accessed, the
major processing steps, what determines the output, and the relevant functions
for key steps.

*Avoid* specific attribute IDs, exact algorithms and detailed conditional logic
- those belong in technical functions.

*Synchronous:* state that the response returns immediately after processing, and
the expected response time if relevant.

*Asynchronous:* what happens immediately on receipt (validation, queueing,
acknowledgement time), the background processing and which function performs it,
how the result reaches the caller (callback URL, notification interface), and
the expected processing time range.
<<<
ERROR_CASES: >>>
TBD - For each:
- **errorCode / type**: when it occurs

Separate immediate errors (validation, authentication) from processing errors,
which an asynchronous interface may report via callback.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: L3-TO
TITLE: Technical interfaces (outbound)

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Interfaces this element **uses** to reach partner elements in the system
context.

**Call behaviour is not specified here.** Timeouts, retry logic and error
handling live in the technical functions that make the calls - see
`CALL_BEHAVIOUR` on the calling step.
<<<

[TECHNICAL_INTERFACE_OUT]
UID: TO-01
CALL_TYPE: Synchronous
STATUS: Draft
PROTOCOL: TBD
TITLE: TBD
STATEMENT: >>>
TBD - Follow the form: "This interface [what it does] by calling [partner
element] ([LINK: PE-01]). Used for [purpose in this element]."

Name the interface for what *this* element does with it, not for what the
partner offers.
<<<
INPUT: >>>
TBD - Every parameter this element must provide:
- **parameterName** (dataType, required/optional): description
<<<
OUTPUT: >>>
TBD - Every value this element receives:
- **outputName** (dataType): description
<<<
ERROR_CASES: >>>
TBD - Every error this element must be prepared to handle:
- **errorCode / type**: what it means
<<<
AUTHORITATIVE_SPEC: >>>
TBD - Where the complete specification lives: the provider element's Element
Design Concept and its inbound interface ID. This document holds the consumer's
view only.
<<<
